        "original_id": "01bd618c-a603-55d7-b818-160036586cd8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steve Gaines, Ronnie Van Zant, Allen Collins, Cassie Gaines\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd\n- Products: Street Survivors, \"That Smell\"\n- Topics: Southern rock\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Gaines was born on September 14, 1949, and he was an American musician.\n- Steve Gaines joined Lynyrd Skynyrd on May 11, 1976, and he was known in the band as a guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter.\n- Street Survivors is the fifth studio album by Southern rock band Lynyrd Skynyrd, and it was released on October 17, 1977.\n- Street Survivors was the last Lynyrd Skynyrd album recorded by original members Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- Street Survivors was the only Lynyrd Skynyrd studio recording to feature guitarist Steve Gaines.\n- \"That Smell\" was written by Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins, and it was released in 1977 on the album Street Survivors.\n- Steve Gaines died on October 20, 1977.\n- Cassie Gaines was Steve Gaines's younger sister, and she was a backup vocalist for Lynyrd Skynyrd's live performances.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
